cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ckepi: Causal Variable Decomposition & Planetary Analog Discovery Engine (Earth · Moon · Mars)"
message: "If you use Ckepi or its causal/statistical analog framework in your research or educational programs, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Lattices Team (Antofagasta Hub — NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AnGeMoNs/Ckepi"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - planetary-analogs
  - mars
  - moon
  - atacama-desert
  - antofagasta
  - h3-spatial-index
  - wasserstein-distance
  - kolmogorov-smirnov
  - open-science
  - nasa-space-apps-2026
abstract: >-
  Open-source planetary analog discovery and STEAM literacy platform that
  decouples independent substrate forcings (X), dependent environmental
  responses (Y), and irreducible physical breakage boundaries (B: gravity,
  atmospheric pressure, ionizing radiation) across a global multi-resolution
  H3 hexagonal grid, paired with common-scale (30 m) non-parametric terrain
  distribution comparisons (Wasserstein-1 and Kolmogorov-Smirnov with 2D
  spatial block bootstrap) and an accessible "Three Worlds for Everyone"
  educational module.
